From be219ad05c5d66e48ed96a9543bb0b17b831be31 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Anselm Busse <anselm.busse@outlook.com>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 22:00:55 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 1/9] x86: restore K1OM support removed in 2.39

Binutils 2.39 dropped the L1OM/K1OM sub-architectures (801a7eab11e,
e961c696dcb, c085ab00c7b).  Bring back the K1OM half: bfd_arch_k1om and
cpu-k1om.c, the elf64-k1om and elf64-k1om-freebsd vectors, the elf_k1om
and elf_k1om_fbsd emulations, -march=k1om and CpuK1OM in gas, and the
tests, as they were in 2.38.  L1OM stays removed.  -march=k1om takes the
CPU_UNKNOWN set (all but IAMCU), which is what "unknown" meant for K1OM
before; i386-gen's dependency table cannot express that as a K1OM entry.

The bfd, opcodes and include parts of binutils knc-2.45 d70aec9302c,
i386 tables regenerated.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: Anselm Busse <anselm.busse@outlook.com>
